  THIS IS A MODIFIED FORK. Files under third_party/libkrun have been changed
  by the Nebula authors and do not correspond to any upstream release. The
  modifications, in the sense of Apache-2.0 section 4(b), are:

    * Snapshot save and restore for krun-backed microVMs — capture of VM,
      vCPU and guest memory state, device-state capture covering transport
      registers and frozen queue configuration, and the matching restore
      loaders using copy-on-write memory mappings.
    * Sparse snapshot memory: all-zero 4 KiB pages are written as file holes.
    * Windows support for the above via the Windows Hypervisor Platform,
      including console re-priming, TSC deadline and IA32_XSS handling on
      restore.
    * linux/arm64 build and release support, with architecture gating around
      the snapshot machinery.
    * Correctness and build fixes: refusing SaveState while a vCPU is running
      (callers must pause first), and a lock-free snapshot_state path after
      save deadlocked on the inner device mutex.

